Article 12
The Regional Government encourages community participation as referred to in Article 6 letter e, by means of:
a. fostering community awareness of cases of violence against women and children;
b. encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting acts of violence against women and children;
c. fostering local wisdom in handling cases of violence;
d. organizing strengthening of community groups in handling acts of violence against women and children;
e. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to acts of violence against women and children.

Article 7
- 7 - (1) The Regional Government shall prevent acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 6 letter a through empowerment and awareness-raising for Families, Parents, and the Community by providing information, guidance and/or outreach.
(2) In addition to the empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), implementation shall be carried out by means of:
a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern toward the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, educational institutions, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; and
g. opening an integrated service system for the protection of women and children from acts of violence in every urban village (kelurahan).

Article 6
The Regional Government in the implementation of Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence as referred to in Article 5 shall carry out:
a. prevention of acts of violence against women and children;
b. legal protection;
c. recovery;
d. coordination; and
e. encouraging community participation.

Article 8
(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 7, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population administration and civil registration;
f. women's empowerment, protection of women and children;
g. cooperatives and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises; and
h. public tranquility, public order, and community protection.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 16
Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of violence against women and children is obligated to:
a. prevent and stop the ongoing act of violence;
b. provide protection to the victim;
c. provide emergency assistance; and/or
d. assist in the process of submitting an application for the determination of protection.

Article 3
The objectives of protecting women and children from acts of violence are to:
a. prevent acts of violence against women and children, including human trafficking;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services to women and children who are victims of violence, to reporters, and to witnesses; and
e. strengthen women and children who are victims of violence so that they are more empowered physically, psychologically, socially, and economically.
